     ttii%%dd:: ffaaiilleedd ttoo eennaabbllee mmeemmoorryy mmaappppiinngg!!  The driver failed to initialize
     PCI shared memory mapping.  This might happen if the card is not in a
     bus-master slot.

     ttii%%dd:: nnoo mmeemmoorryy ffoorr jjuummbboo bbuuffffeerrss!!  The driver failed to allocate memory
     for jumbo frames during initialization.

     ttii%%dd:: bbiiooss tthhiinnkkss wwee''rree iinn aa 6644 bbiitt sslloott,, bbuutt wwee aarreenn''tt  The BIOS has
     programmed the NIC as though it had been installed in a 64-bit PCI slot,
     but in fact the NIC is in a 32-bit slot.  This happens as a result of a
     bug in some BIOSes.  This can be worked around on the Tigon II, but on
     the Tigon I initialization will fail.

     ttii%%dd:: bbooaarrdd sseellff--ddiiaaggnnoossttiiccss ffaaiilleedd!!  The ROMFAIL bit in the CPU state
